# Lint rule waivers for the plain Verilog-2001 sources in this directory.
#
# Verible's default rule set encodes a SystemVerilog style guide, and it
# applies that guide to `.v' files too -- IEEE 1364 was folded into IEEE
# 1800 in 2009, so as far as the tool is concerned there is one language.
# The four rules below are waived for two different reasons. The first
# three ask for constructs that DO NOT EXIST in Verilog-2001, so obeying
# them here would mean giving up the thing this directory exists to
# show; the fourth (`parameter-name-style') is not about a missing
# construct at all -- it is a SystemVerilog style-guide naming
# preference, waived because applying it would misrepresent Verilog-2001
# convention as a style deficiency:
#
#   explicit-parameter-storage-type   wants `parameter int unsigned W'
#                                     -- typed parameters are SV-only.
#   explicit-task-lifetime            wants `task automatic' -- SV-only.
#   unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
#                                     wants `reg mem [DEPTH]' -- the
#                                     `[0:DEPTH-1]' form is the Verilog
#                                     one, and still legal.
#   parameter-name-style              its `parameter_style' allows both
#                                     CamelCase and ALL_CAPS, so plain
#                                     `parameter' declarations (as in
#                                     fifo_sync.v) already pass with no
#                                     waiver; what actually fails is
#                                     `localparam_style', which is
#                                     CamelCase-only and rejects a
#                                     multi-word ALL_CAPS `localparam'
#                                     (fifo_sync_tb.v's `localparam
#                                     DATA_WIDTH' / `ADDR_WIDTH'; the
#                                     single-word `localparam DEPTH'
#                                     passes on its own). UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
#                                     is the universal Verilog-2001
#                                     convention for both, so renaming the
#                                     localparams to satisfy this rule
#                                     would misrepresent what this code is
#                                     meant to show.
#
# Waiving per-directory rather than globally is deliberate: the
# SystemVerilog design under demo/rtl/ passes the full default rule set
# with no waivers at all, and should keep having to.

-explicit-parameter-storage-type
-explicit-task-lifetime
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
-parameter-name-style
